      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-136536",
      ":question/problem": "The height above the ground of a seat on a Ferris wheel, in feet, is modeled by a function of the form $H(t) = A\\cos (Bt) + C$, where $A$, $B$, $C$ are constants, and $t$ is the time (in seconds) since the wheel started the ride.\n\nIt is observed that when $t = 0$, the seat is $2$ feet off the ground, the lowest height it can reach. The maximum height of $32$ feet is reached $20$ seconds after the wheel has started to rotate.\n\nWhich of the following could be the function $H(t)$?"
