      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-136656",
      ":question/problem": "A weight attached to a spring bounces up and down so that its height from the ground, in inches, can be modeled by a function of the form $H(t) = A\\sin (Bt) + C$, where $A$, $B$, $C$ are constants, and $t$ is the time (in seconds) since the motion begins.\n\nIt is observed that when $t = 0$, the weight is halfway between its minimum and maximum heights. The minimum height of $4$ inches is reached after $0.5$ seconds. The maximum height reached by the weight is $8$ inches.\n\nWhich of the following could be the function $H(t)$?"
